<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <base href="/" />
    <title>Blow lazy loading sample</title>
    @* Linked by hand, as in every app: Blow does not inject its stylesheet. It is a static web asset, not part of
       Bit.Blow.wasm, so it is served before the assembly is downloaded and the canvas is laid out from its first
       render. app.css comes after it, so the sample's own rules win. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["_content/Bit.Blow/bit-blow.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    @* Without an icon the browser asks for /favicon.ico, and the 404 lands in the console the end-to-end tests check. *@
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="@Assets["favicon.svg"]" />
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />
</head>

<body>
    @* The router runs in the browser, where its OnNavigateAsync downloads Bit.Blow.wasm before the workflow renders. *@
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />
    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
